^renv$
^renv\.lock$
^data-raw$
^codemeta\.json$
^_pkgdown\.yml$
^docs$
^CONTRIBUTING\.md$
^CODE_OF_CONDUCT\.md$
^CITATION\.cff$
^CITATION\.bib$
^\.github$
^LICENSE\.md$
# NOTE: every line here is compiled as a Perl regex, comments included -- roxygen2
# errors on an uncompilable line. Keep comment prose free of regex metacharacters:
# no parentheses, brackets, braces, pipes or leading quantifiers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo-level data inputs, NOT package datasets. Scripts, the shiny app and
# SHA256SUMS.txt address these by literal repo path, and their SHA-256s are pinned
# in data/PROVENANCE_vendored_inputs.md. Shipping them as a data/ directory makes
# R CMD check treat the .csv as an undocumented dataset and reject the .rds and .md
# as disallowed types. Excluded from the build; the repo paths are untouched.
^data$
# Repo-integrity suite, not a package test suite: most files readLines or source
# the R/ and scripts/ SOURCE files by path -- SSOT guards that grep the code itself
# for constants. Those inputs do not exist in an installed package, so the suite
# cannot run under R CMD check. It stays the documented local gate:
# Rscript tests/testthat.R
^tests$
# Repo tooling and root anchors -- not part of the installed package.
^\.here$
^\.renvignore$
^manuscript$
^scripts$
^artifacts$
^tools$
^render\.R$
^render_docx\.R$
^SHA256SUMS\.txt$
^CHANGELOG\.md$
# Analysis scripts in Python, added alongside the secondary-location sensitivity
# work. They sit at the repo root and are not package content -- same status as
# render.R and the scripts directory above. Without this, R CMD check reports
# them under "checking top-level files" as a NOTE, which the nightly treats as a
# failure. Pattern rather than two literal names so the next one is covered too;
# it is anchored so it only matches the package ROOT, never R/ or tools/.
^[^/]+\.py$
# Generated pkgdown output. Never package content; would otherwise be reported
# by R CMD check under "checking top-level files", which the nightly fails on.
^pkgdown-site$
^\.zenodo\.json$
